Yet Another Extremely Stupid Death.

Boy, am I ever mad at myself.

Chaotic wizard, DL 26, hadn't reached Medusa yet and was getting bored
and, as a consequence beginning to play rather carelessly. I was at
XL16, had all the resistances *except* disintegration, and no source
of reflection. (You see where this is going?) I had the Eye of the
Aethiopica, was wielding the +2 Magicbane and had finger of death at
0% fail, and as a result thought myself invulnerable.

Mapping out DL26, I was running down a corridor (Control-running, not
Shift-running, which makes it a little less stupid, but still...) when
I ran right into the disintegration beam of a black dragon. The thing
was, it missed me. This is why I feel really stupid.

I could have teleported right beside it and killed it with Magicbane
-- I knew dragons don't use their breath weapons from close up. I
could have teleported away. I could have dug a hole and dropped
through it. I could have zapped it with Finger of Death (though I
suppose that could have missed). But like the overconfident idiot I
was, I decided that this was a good time to see whether black dragons
were resistant to sleep rays. I *still* don't know whether they are or
not, because the sleep ray missed and the next thing I knew, my cloak
and shirt had disintegrated, and the DYWYPI? prompt came up. I sat
there for a moment, staring at the screen in total disbelief. I was so
sure I was going to ascend this one.

To give myself what little credit I deserve, I *was* under the
impression that a disintegration beam only disintegrated one piece of
armor at once, and only disintegrated *you* if you weren't wearing any
armor. Since I was wearing five pieces of armor (but no body armor) at
the time, I felt I was safe for at least five moves. But even so
that's no excuse.

Oh, well...back to square one...(and after all that tedious
sacrificing and praying, too...)

